  "discussion": {
    "headline": "nother week of sunny, dry and beautiful weather!",
    "dateLine": "12:30 p.m. Tuesday, November 17, 2026",
    "excerpt": "Last Friday, the high temperature failed to reach 60°F at Millersville University for the first time this fall. Previously, the latest date for the first sub-60°F high temperature since 1914 was November 1st. Ironically, the high temperature also failed to reach 50°F last Friday, and the feat was then repeated on Saturday. A deep trough, or dip in the Jet Stream, over the eastern U.S. …",
